WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.278 --> 00:00:03.993
(mysterious music)

00:00:03.993 --> 00:00:05.009
- [Leslie Voiceover]
I've always been drawn

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:07.530
to abandoned and forgotten places.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:10.577
(camera shutter clicks)
(mysterious music)

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:13.254
Behind every door there's a story.

00:00:13.254 --> 00:00:14.543
(camera shutter clicks)
(mysterious music)

00:00:14.543 --> 00:00:17.288
Every room and every object
has something to say.

00:00:17.288 --> 00:00:19.279
(camera shutter clicks)
(mysterious music)

00:00:19.279 --> 00:00:20.913
You never know what you’re going to find

00:00:20.913 --> 00:00:22.021
or who you'll find.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:24.649
(mysterious music)

00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:26.290
My name is Leslie Muir.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.496
I photograph and explore abandoned places

00:00:28.496 --> 00:00:29.999
in Ontario, Canada.

00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:33.316
(camera shutter clicks)
(mysterious music)

00:00:33.316 --> 00:00:35.816
(light music)

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.806
Any time I go to an abandoned house

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:43.507
there's still an energy, there's
still a story to be told.

00:00:43.507 --> 00:00:45.261
You can feel it from the
time you step out of your car

00:00:45.261 --> 00:00:46.742
on that driveway,

00:00:46.742 --> 00:00:49.575
and that's the beauty of it,
the beauty is the unknown.

00:00:49.575 --> 00:00:52.475
(mysterious music)

00:00:52.475 --> 00:00:54.987
About a year ago I was driving home,

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:57.279
had seen this house a million times,

00:00:57.279 --> 00:01:01.879
never thought to stop, it was just
another abandoned house.

00:01:01.879 --> 00:01:04.430
For some reason I did a U-turn
in the middle of the road,

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.705
and I got out of my car
and started taking pictures

00:01:07.705 --> 00:01:09.522
of the outside.

00:01:09.522 --> 00:01:11.738
When I went inside it was
still an abandoned house to me.

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:14.160
It was dark, there was stuff everywhere,

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.501
any sign that you saw would
have led you to believe

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.105
that nobody had lived there,

00:01:18.105 --> 00:01:20.879
it was an abandoned home.

00:01:20.879 --> 00:01:24.093
I heard a radio and a timid
hello from the corner,

00:01:24.093 --> 00:01:25.992
and I met Lawrence.

00:01:25.992 --> 00:01:26.825
(camera shutter clicks)

00:01:26.825 --> 00:01:28.750
(anxious piano music)

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.314
He looked tired, he looked lonely.

00:01:31.314 --> 00:01:32.991
He had a fractured hip.

00:01:32.991 --> 00:01:34.281
He was missing one eye.

00:01:34.281 --> 00:01:36.633
He was in a pretty rough shape.

00:01:36.633 --> 00:01:38.192
I thought, "Here's your chance

00:01:38.192 --> 00:01:40.246
"to be there for somebody who needs it."

00:01:40.246 --> 00:01:43.579
(inspiring piano music)

00:01:44.507 --> 00:01:48.719
It started with some visits,
getting to know each other,

00:01:48.719 --> 00:01:50.744
and now we're genuinely friends.

00:01:50.744 --> 00:01:54.077
(camera shutter clicks)

00:02:01.759 --> 00:02:03.149
- [Leslie Voiceover] It's
really hard to find somebody

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:05.181
that you can genuinely
trust in this world,

00:02:05.181 --> 00:02:06.680
somebody who is not gonna judge you.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:10.597
He has made me realize
what's really important.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:19.027
(melancholic piano music)

00:02:19.027 --> 00:02:19.968
- [Leslie Voiceover] People takes pictures

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:22.017
of what they care about,
of what they're proud of,

00:02:22.017 --> 00:02:23.748
of what they want to remember.

00:02:23.748 --> 00:02:25.659
Nobody takes a picture of something

00:02:25.659 --> 00:02:28.169
that they want to forget.

00:02:28.169 --> 00:02:32.262
So, I try to take his picture
as often as possible now.

00:02:32.262 --> 00:02:33.368
(camera shutter clicks)

00:02:33.368 --> 00:02:36.868
(melancholic piano music)

